  47: 
  48:     Input structure
  49:     - The black background contains one or more 4-connected green outline objects.
  50:     - Each green object has a bounding box with exactly one side containing a single green tab pixel.
  51:     - The intended reflected copy is separated from the original bounding box by one background row or column and may be clipped by the grid edge.
  52: 
  53:     Rule
  54:     - If the tab is on the left or right, mirror the object horizontally and place it on the opposite side in blue.
  55:     - If the tab is on the top or bottom, mirror the object vertically and place it on the opposite side in teal.
  56:     - Keep every original green pixel unchanged and paint only background cells reached by the reflected copy.
  57: 
  58:     Key insight
  59:     - The lone boundary pixel identifies both the mirror axis and the side to avoid; the copy appears across the object's opposite bbox side with a one-cell gap.
  60:     """
