  17:     Extend each control pixel perpendicular to the full bars, marking every bar hit with a 3x3 contact marker.
  18: 
  19:     Input structure
  20:     - The background is the dominant color.
  21:     - Exactly one foreground color forms one or more complete parallel rows or complete parallel columns.
  22:     - The other foreground color appears as isolated control pixels off those bars.
  23: 
  24:     Rule
  25:     - For each control pixel, cast rays in both directions perpendicular to the bars.
  26:     - Stop each ray at the first bar cell it reaches and color the control-to-hit segment with the control color.
  27:     - After all rays are drawn, stamp a 3x3 block of the bar color centered on each hit, restoring the center to the control color.
  28:     - Directions with no bar before the grid edge emit nothing.
  29: 
  30:     Key insight
  31:     - The only complete rows or columns identify the bars and their orientation; the contact markers are layered after the rays.
  32:     """
  33:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
  34:     H, W = g.shape
  35:     bg = get_bg(g)
  36:     colors = colors_present(g, exclude={bg})
  37: 
  38:     bar_candidates: list[tuple[int, list[int], list[int]]] = []
  39:     for color in colors:
  40:         rows, cols = _complete_lines(g, color)
  41:         if rows or cols:
  42:             bar_candidates.append((color, rows, cols))
  43: 
  44:     assert len(bar_candidates) == 1
  45:     bar_color, bar_rows, bar_cols = bar_candidates[0]
  46:     assert bool(bar_rows) ^ bool(bar_cols)
  47: 
  48:     control_colors = [color for color in colors if color != bar_color]
  49:     assert len(control_colors) == 1
  50:     control_color = control_colors[0]
  51:     controls = np.argwhere(g == control_color)
  52:     assert len(controls) > 0
  53: 
  54:     out = g.copy()
  55:     hits: set[tuple[int, int]] = set()
  56: 
  57:     if bar_rows:
  58:         for r0, c0 in controls:
  59:             r = int(r0)
  60:             c = int(c0)
  61:             for dr in (-1, 1):
  62:                 rr = r + dr
  63:                 while 0 <= rr < H:
  64:                     if g[rr, c] == bar_color:
  65:                         lo, hi = sorted((r, rr))
  66:                         out[lo : hi + 1, c] = control_color
  67:                         hits.add((rr, c))
  68:                         break
  69:                     rr += dr
  70:     else:
  71:         for r0, c0 in controls:
  72:             r = int(r0)
  73:             c = int(c0)
  74:             for dc in (-1, 1):
  75:                 cc = c + dc
  76:                 while 0 <= cc < W:
